<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#yang-di-pertuan-agong">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1957">1957</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as King of Malaysia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yang di-Pertuan Agong is the head of state of Malaysia, a constitutional monarch elected for a five-year term by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-rulers">Conference of Rulers</a> from among the nine hereditary rulers of the Malay states. The office was created at independence in 1957, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuanku-abdul-rahman">Tuanku Abdul Rahman</a> of Negeri Sembilan became the first holder. In practice the throne rotates among the states, and the king acts on the advice of the government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong.jpg" alt="Yang di-Pertuan Agong" width="320" height="303" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_Yang_di-Pertuan_Agong_of_Malaysia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
